# Political Landscape Cartography — .gitignore
#
# What this file does:
#   - Excludes OS / editor / AI-tooling junk that should never be committed
#   - Excludes operator-private environment + secrets files
#   - DOES NOT exclude any PLC engine, framework, Prototype, template, or scaffolding content
#   - DOES NOT exclude sphere cartridges by default (the audit trail is the value;
#     sphere cartridges should be committed to the operator's own repo)
#
# Per-sphere customization:
#   Each sphere may add its own `.gitignore` inside `Spheres/<sphere-name>/`
#   to exclude sphere-specific operator-private content (e.g., principal-eyes-only
#   draft notes, sealed export artifacts). See `OPERATOR-GUIDE.md` for guidance.

# ============================================================
# Operating system junk
# ============================================================
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ============================================================
# Editor and IDE state
# ============================================================
# Vim
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.netrwhist

# Emacs
\#*\#
.\#*

# VS Code (workspace-local; user-specific)
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# JetBrains
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws

# Sublime Text
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project

# Obsidian per-user UI state (the vault config itself should be committed if shared;
# the workspace state is local)
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspaces.json

# ============================================================
# AI tooling state
# ============================================================
# Claude Code session state (session-specific; should not propagate)
.claude/
.claude.json

# Cursor IDE
.cursor/

# GitHub Copilot
.copilot/

# Generic AI session caches
.ai-cache/
.chatcache/

# ============================================================
# Environment + secrets
# ============================================================
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.envrc

# Common secret file patterns — these should NEVER appear in a PLC OV folder,
# but the exclusion is defense-in-depth
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
*.secret

# ============================================================
# Backup + temporary files
# ============================================================
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.tmp
*.temp
*~

# ============================================================
# Personal source materials — DO NOT SYNC
# ============================================================
# The Lam 2018 Pepperdine dissertation PDF is the Methodology Author's
# personal academic work. It stays local in the operator's working copy of
# this OV folder, but it is NEVER pushed to any remote (GitHub or otherwise).
# Anyone who needs the dissertation source contacts the Methodology Author
# directly per `_frameworks/sources/Lam-2018-Pepperdine.md` (the request
# placeholder, which DOES sync).
_frameworks/sources/Lam-2018-Pepperdine.pdf

# ============================================================
# Log files
# ============================================================
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ============================================================
# Archive + compressed files
# ============================================================
# (Operators occasionally extract zips into the OV folder by accident)
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.rar
*.7z

# ============================================================
# OS-generated files in specific tools
# ============================================================
# Python virtualenvs (in case operator uses scripts alongside PLC)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Node (in case any tooling lives alongside)
node_modules/
.npm/

# ============================================================
# Worktree state from this PLC's own design history
# ============================================================
# (Specific to the design-time OVE workflow; do not commit OVE design state
# into a deployed PLC OV)
.ove-design-state/

# ============================================================
# Export artifacts (operator-discretion)
# ============================================================
# Generated EXPORT-SHAREABLE artifacts that contain redacted but still
# sensitive client material. By default, these are NOT excluded — the operator
# should commit them as part of the audit trail. If the operator's threat
# model requires excluding them, uncomment:
#
# Spheres/*/exports/

# ============================================================
# WHAT WE DO NOT EXCLUDE (preserved verbatim)
# ============================================================
# - All engine zone:        _plc-engine/
# - All Prototypes:         _Prototypes/
# - All framework zone:     _frameworks/ + _PATTERNS/
# - All scaffolding zone:   _plc-engine/_templates/ + _plc-engine/_yaml/
# - All root documentation: README, INSTALL, OPERATOR-GUIDE, CONTRIBUTING,
#                           LICENSE, VERSION, CHANGELOG, AI-BOOTSTRAP,
#                           BOOTSTRAP-NEW-SPHERE, UPDATE-PROMPT
# - All sphere cartridges:  Spheres/  (the audit trail is the value)
#
# If you have a specific reason to exclude one of these, add the exclusion
# in a per-sphere .gitignore inside Spheres/<sphere>/.gitignore — not here.
# Modifications to this root-level .gitignore should be limited to operator-
# universal exclusions (junk files; secrets patterns).
